# Literals this repo publishes ON PURPOSE, suppressed wherever they appear.
#
# scripts/check-public-repo-secrets.py matches these by VALUE, in any file, in
# any category. That is deliberately different from .secret-allowlist, which
# suppresses by `file` / `file:line` / `file::CATEGORY`.
#
# Why a value list is needed at all: the build-output scan. A public identifier
# is rendered into EVERY page, so suppressing it by path would need one entry
# per built page, and every one of them would go stale the next time the build
# renumbers a line or adds a page. Attaching the suppression to the value keeps
# it correct across a rebuild and stops it widening to cover a different secret
# that happens to share a file.
#
# The bar for an entry here is high, and it is not "this is not a credential".
# It is: THIS EXACT STRING IS ALREADY PUBLIC, served to anyone who views the
# site. If a value is merely low-risk, or internal, or "probably fine", it does
# not belong here -- put it in .env and reference it as an environment variable.
#
# Anything not listed is still a finding. The list fails in the safe direction.

# Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon token.
#
# PUBLIC BY DESIGN. It is a site identifier, not a credential: it ships inside
# every page's rendered HTML (layouts/_partials/head.html), so it is visible in
# view-source to every visitor. Holding it grants nothing -- it identifies which
# site a page-view belongs to and cannot read the analytics data back.
#
# It is allowlisted at source as `layouts/_partials/head.html:128`, but that
# entry is line-anchored to the ONE template line. The build renders the token
# into ~350 pages, so the built-output scan needs it suppressed by value.
